{
  "manufacturer": "Intesis (HMS Networks)",
  "manufacturer_slug": "intesis",
  "model": "INMBSSAM016O000 Samsung NASA (R1/R2) VRF to Modbus gateway (4 to 64 units)",
  "model_slug": "inmbssam016o000",
  "short_model": "INMBSSAM016O000 Samsung NASA",
  "aliases": [
    "INMBSSAM004O000",
    "INMBSSAM008O000",
    "INMBSSAM016O000",
    "INMBSSAM064O000",
    "SM-ACN-MBS-4",
    "SM-ACN-MBS-8",
    "SM-ACN-MBS-16",
    "SM-ACN-MBS-64"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VRF / split AC gateway",
  "applies_to": "Intesis Modbus Server - Samsung NASA, order codes INMBSSAM004O000 / 008O000 / 016O000 / 064O000 (legacy SM-ACN-MBS-4/8/16/64), user manual r1.4 (12/2020); Samsung NASA R1/R2 bus.",
  "summary": "Modbus server on the Samsung NASA R1/R2 bus covering indoor units, AHUs, ERVs, EHS / hydro units and chillers. Each configured unit gets a 100-register block; outdoor unit communication flags and all-unit commands sit at the bottom of the map. Modbus RTU and TCP run together.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The manual states formula results are link-layer addresses with the first register at 0. Unit index Ui (1..64, from the MAPS Units Configuration tab) uses Ui x 100 + offset; outdoor unit address OU (0..15) is its own register 0..15. This file lists Ui = 1 (100..140) and OU 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Intesis Modbus Server - Samsung NASA User Manual",
    "doc_number": "User Manual r1.4 EN",
    "revision_date": "2020-12",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-inmbssamxxxo000.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 8-11 (Modbus interface and address map)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Only unit index 1 is listed. For index Ui add (Ui-1) x 100. Outdoor unit communication error sits at register = OU address (0..15).",
    "Available registers depend on the unit type chosen in MAPS (IU, HE, HT, EHS, AHU, ERV, ERV+, chiller); the manual's type matrix is not reproduced.",
    "Ambient temperature (Ui*100+5) is left out: unlike every other temperature in the map it has no x10 marker (range -41..100 °C), so its scale is not clear.",
    "Temperatures are tenths of °C.",
    "Mode register (Ui*100+1) codes by unit type: IU/AHU 0 Auto, 1 Heat, 2 Dry, 3 Fan, 4 Cool; HE 1 Heat, 4 Cool; EHS/ERV+ 0 Auto, 1 Heat, 4 Cool; chiller 1 Heat, 4 Cool, 5 Cool Storage, 6 Heat Storage."
  ],
